<article class="env-lemma" id="8A354F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8A354F">Lemma <span data-tag="8A354F">5.4.5.12</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal, and let $f: \calI \rightarrow \calJ $ be an $\kappa $-cofinal map of filtered $\infty $-categories. Then $f$ is cofinal. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Theorem <a href="/tag/A37F6A" data-tag="A37F6A">4.1.3.1</a>, to prove that $f$ is cofinal it suffices to show that for every object $J \in \calJ $, the fiber product $\calI _{J/} = \calI \times _{\calJ } \calJ _{J/}$ is weakly contractible. Lemma <a href="/tag/98C19B" data-tag="98C19B">5.4.5.11</a> asserts that $\calI _{J/}$ is $\kappa $-filtered; now apply Lemma <a href="/tag/701AD3" data-tag="701AD3">5.3.1.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>